cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Machine-checked bounds on K(8,1,2), the first unknown term of OEIS A004045"
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
version: "2.2"
date-released: "2026-09-02"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22217672"
authors:
  - given-names: Hanyu
    family-names: Yang
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-0419-4070"
abstract: >-
  Artifacts for lower bounds on binary multiple covering codes. An elementary
  parity/excess argument shows that for even n every binary code whose closed
  radius-1 balls cover each point at least twice satisfies
  |C| >= ceil(3 * 2^(n+1) / (3n+2)). This strictly improves the best published
  lower bound on K(n,1,2) at n = 8, 10, 12, 14 and 16, and reproves the exact
  value K(6,1,2) = 20 without computer search. In particular K(8,1,2) >= 60,
  one above the published lower bound, established by three independent routes.
  The package also refutes |C| = 60, giving K(8,1,2) >= 61, and formalises that
  refutation in Lean 4 with zero sorry's and an audited axiom trace, alongside
  machine-checkable certificates. Hence 61 <= K(8,1,2) <= 64. A further result,
  on a weaker footing, indicates that every twofold covering of F_2^8 with at
  most 63 codewords has trivial automorphism group. No human has reviewed the
  proof or the Lean definitions.
keywords:
  - covering codes
  - multiple covering codes
  - Hamming space
  - OEIS A004045
  - double domination
  - hypercube
  - Delsarte inequalities
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
  - certified computation
